Q: Making an array that accepts only a string and instances of a class? A: <p>You can use the base class <code>DialogueCommand</code> as a container for a string and use implicit conversion operator:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>class DialogueCommand()
{
    protected readonly string? str;
    public DialogueCommand(string str) : this() =&gt; this.str = str;
    public static implicit operator DialogueCommand(string str) =&gt; new(str);
}

class SetImage(string str) : DialogueCommand(str) { }
class PlayMusic(string str) : DialogueCommand(str) { }
class StopMusic : DialogueCommand { }

return new DialogueCommand[]
{
    &quot;this is an example line with two commands!&quot;, new SetImage(&quot;image3&quot;), new PlayMusic(&quot;example&quot;),
    &quot;line without commands&quot;,
    // ...
    &quot;and that's how the lines are made!&quot;, new StopMusic()
};
</code></pre>
